# mousemix: the shared decoded-event queue proof.  readKey AND readMouse are
# BOTH armed, and one send carries keys and a mouse event INTERLEAVED.  Every
# event must be delivered to the right reader (no drop, no mis-route):
#   'a' -> K:a,  \e[<0;2;1M (cb=0 left, cx=2 cy=1) -> M:press:left@1,0,  'b' -> K:b
# Separate expects (substring) prove all three events landed; the queue's
# routing is what maps each byte run to the right reader.
expect READY
send a\e[<0;2;1Mb
expect K:a
expect M:press:left@1,0
expect K:b
send q
expect_exit 0
